    "question": {
      ":question/id": "7a1618e0-c03d-5081-bf8b-dab6ee107a0e",
      ":question/problem": "Which of the numbers below belong to $\\mathbb{R}_0^{-}$?\n\nSelect all that apply.",
      ":question/worked-solution": "Remember that $\\mathbb{R}_0^{-}$ is the set of all negative real numbers and zero.\n\n- $\\sqrt{9}=3$: It is positive, and it is an integer. Therefore, it does *not* belong to $\\mathbb{R}_0^{-}$.\n\n- $\\pi$: It is positive, and it is an irrational real number. Therefore, it does *not* belong to $\\mathbb{R}_0^{-}$.\n\n- $0$: Zero is included by the subscript $0$. Therefore, it belongs to $\\mathbb{R}_0^{-}$.\n\n- $-2$: It is negative, and it is an integer. Therefore, it belongs to $\\mathbb{R}_0^{-}$.\n\nIn conclusion, the correct answer is: $0$; $-2$.",
      ":question/difficulty": ":question.difficulty/easy",
