      ":question/problem": "Which of the numbers below belong to $\\mathbb{Q}^{-}$?\n\nSelect all that apply.",
      ":question/worked-solution": "Remember that $\\mathbb{Q}^{-}$ is the set of all negative rational numbers.\n\n- $\\sqrt{28}=2\\sqrt{7}$: It is positive, and it is an irrational real number. Therefore, it does *not* belong to $\\mathbb{Q}^{-}$.\n\n- $\\sqrt{24}=2\\sqrt{6}$: It is positive, and it is an irrational real number. Therefore, it does *not* belong to $\\mathbb{Q}^{-}$.\n\n- $-44$: It is negative, and it is an integer. Therefore, it belongs to $\\mathbb{Q}^{-}$.\n\n- $\\frac{27}{5}$: It is positive, and it is a rational number but not an integer. Therefore, it does *not* belong to $\\mathbb{Q}^{-}$.\n\nIn conclusion, the correct answer is: $-44$.",
