      ":question/worked-solution": "Remember that $\\mathbb{R}_0^{+}$ is the set of all positive real numbers and zero.\n\n- $-53$: It is negative, and it is an integer. Therefore, it does *not* belong to $\\mathbb{R}_0^{+}$.\n\n- $-\\sqrt{44}=-2\\sqrt{11}$: It is negative, and it is an irrational real number. Therefore, it does *not* belong to $\\mathbb{R}_0^{+}$.\n\n- $\\frac{33}{7}$: It is positive, and it is a rational number but not an integer. Therefore, it belongs to $\\mathbb{R}_0^{+}$.\n\n- $-\\frac{35}{5}=-7$: It is negative, and it is an integer. Therefore, it does *not* belong to $\\mathbb{R}_0^{+}$.\n\nIn conclusion, the correct answer is: $\\frac{33}{7}$.",
